<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#hebrew">Glossary</a> · Term · language</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hebrew</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hebrew is a Semitic language, the language of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a> and of ancient Israel. Hebrew scripture records the impact of Assyrian, Babylonian and Chaldean power on the kingdoms of Israel and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a>. The Carthaginian title of suffete shares a Semitic root with Hebrew shofet, judge, and Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-ii-of-brazil">Pedro II</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> translated works from Hebrew.</p></div>
